From fb8ce3569543261caa99ddb0d806eba071f0e951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:39:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(gateway): a completion note waits out another
 turn's lease; recover failed completion admissions

An async delegation's ledger row is acknowledged `delivered` when its admission commits. On the
MacBook (deleg_e757744d, admission ca1d8f79) the admitted note then met a turn lease another turn
held on the parent conversation; SessionTurnLeaseLostError settled the admission `failed` and the
result never reached the parent. A request id is admitted once, so a re-offer resolved to that
failed admission and was "acknowledged" again without delivering anything.

- session_completion_notes: the FIFO head's note write retries (backoff 0.25-2 s, a warning per
  minute) while another turn holds the lease, re-reading the physical tip each try. The note is
  keyed by its admission, so a refused try leaves nothing to repeat. Cancellation still stops it.
- completion_admission_recovery (new): once per gateway start the async-delegation watcher scans
  the newest 200 `failed` local completion admissions; for each with no note (by
  completion_admission) and no copy of its text in the target session, it reopens every carried
  delegation via requeue_admitted_completion. The claimed offer (claim_completion_delivery stays the
  gate) reaches `deliver_admitted`, which writes the failed admission's note keyed by that admission
  (exactly once); a refused write releases the claim, spending an attempt, so the row converges to
  `dropped` with a logged reason. Any other existing admission is the lost ACK it always was.
- requeue_admitted_completion: a row past _MAX_COMPLETION_REPLAY_AGE_S is dropped with a WARNING
  naming the delegation instead of being reopened and then skipped silently by _replay_pending.

Tests: test_completion_note_turn_lease (RED on 2cfdbeedc2: admission settles while the lease is
held), test_completion_admission_reconcile (RED without the recovery: no note / row stays pending;
negative controls: a completed admission or an existing note is never reopened).
